97% of actively publishing climate scientists agree that current warming is primarily caused by human greenhouse gas emissions, according to a 2013 analysis of 11,944 peer-reviewed papers.
Atmospheric CO₂ has risen from 280 ppm pre-industrial to over 422 ppm in 2024 — higher than at any point in the last 800,000 years, as shown by Antarctic ice core records.
The IPCC Sixth Assessment Report (2021), authored by 234 scientists from 66 countries, concluded it is 'unequivocal' that human influence has warmed the climate.
Every major scientific organisation on Earth — NASA, NOAA, the Royal Society, the Chinese Academy of Sciences — has issued statements affirming the human cause of current warming.
